You can use this hook in your component to handle adding items to the cart globally:

```jsx
// useCart.js
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { addItem } from './cartSlice';

export const useCart = () => {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();
  return (item) => dispatch(addItem(item));
};
```

Then in your UI:

```jsx
// ProductCard.js
import { useCart } from '../hooks/useCart';

function ProductCard({ product }) {
  const addToCart = useCart();
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{product.name}</h2>
      <p>${product.price}</p>
      <button onClick={() => addToCart(product)}>Add to Cart</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

You can use this same pattern with `removeItem` for the cart view.

```jsx
const CartComponent = () => {
  const { items } = useSelector(state => state.cart);
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  return (
    <div>
      {items.map(item => (
        <div key={item.id}>
          {item.name} - {item.price}
          <button onClick={() => dispatch(removeItem(item.id))}>Remove</button>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

That's the core. You'd add quantity controls and totals based on your needs. The cart slice handles the business logic, this just renders it.

